{"result":"{
  "total": -1,
  "start_at": 0,
  "max_results": 10,
  "issues": [
    {
      "id": "18434",
      "key": "SFCC-238",
      "summary": "Spike: Contentful-to-PWA Kit Product/Category ID Rendering (Hook Integration)",
      "description": "Objective\nDocument how SFCC Product and Category IDs authored in a Contentful content model are resolved to rendered commerce data in the PWA Kit — specifically which \n@salesforce/commerce-sdk-react\n hook is called, where that hook lives, and how the ID key passes from the Contentful entry into the hook — so the squad has one confirmed pattern to reuse across every content type that embeds a product or category reference (product spotlights, Shop the Look, PLP inline grid inserts, mega-menu tiles).\nBackground\nThe Contentful App for SFCC (Salesforce Commerce Cloud connector) is now installed, letting content authors pick SFCC product/category IDs directly inside Contentful entries. A working single-product bridge already exists in the codebase — \nproductHero.tsx\n and the ShoppableImage hotspots both pass a Contentful \nproductId\n string into \nuseProduct\n — but it was built against a mock space using plain string fields, resolves client-side, and has no category or multi-product equivalent. SFCC-123 (Contentful Integration TSD) documents the page-scoping filter pattern but explicitly leaves reference-resolution / hook-wiring open; this spike closes that gap. Note the existing bridge calls \nuseProduct\n inside leaf components, which conflicts with the container/presentational rule and the SSR-first/LCP mandate — this needs an explicit ruling. Angelo to align with the SFCC-123 owner (Jhoan) and the incoming Contentful squad.\nTasks\nDocument the existing product-ID → hook bridge (\nuseProduct\n in \nproductHero.tsx\n and \nhotspotPopup.tsx\n) and the \nproductId\n convention (\nSFCC_PRODUCT_ID_FIELD\n) as the current-state baseline\nDetermine how the newly-installed Contentful App for SFCC surfaces product/category references (field type and payload shape) and map that to the commerce hook's key parameter\nDefine the confirmed resolution mechanic: which hook per reference type (\nuseProduct\n for products; \nuseCategory\n / \nuseProductSearch\n for the category gap), where it is called (SSR container vs leaf component), and how the ID passes through\nReconcile the pattern with the container/presentational rule and the SSR-first / ≤2s p75 mobile LCP budget — rule on client-side hook vs SSR fetch-and-pass-down\nCover the reference variants missing today: category references (no bridge exists) and multiple/array product references (single \nproductId\n only)\nConfirm product name/price ownership (Contentful vs SFCC) to close HPC-001, since the pattern assumes IDs in Contentful and all commerce data resolved from SFCC\nDefinition of Done\nA Technical Solution Document (following the official 8-section TSD template) is produced and signed off per Section 8, documenting the confirmed reference-resolution pattern — which hook, where it is called, and how the Contentful ID key is passed — validated for both product and category references and for single and multiple references, reconciled with the SSR-first and container/presentational rules, and sufficient for the squad to build any embedded-reference content type consistently.",
      "status": {
        "name": "Ready for Development",
        "category": "To Do",
        "color": "blue-gray"
      },
      "issue_type": {
        "name": "Spike"
      },
      "labels": [
        "Squad-A"
      ],
      "updated": "2026-07-31T19:17:09.107+1000"
    },
    {
      "id": "18361",
      "key": "SFCC-195",
      "summary": "PDP – Slide Out - Details & Care",
      "description": "As a\n Shopper,\nI want\n to access detailed product information in an organised, expandable format on the PDP,\nso that\n I can find the information I need without leaving the product page.\nImage for reference (Figma is leading):\nAfter clicking on the CTA (e.g. “Details & Care), then this slide out selecting the relevant tab that was clicked:\nThe PDP displays a set of tabs on the slide out, corresponding with the CTAs. Each tab expands inline to reveal its content.\nScope:\nThis user story is only for the slide out component and the first Details & Care tab (other tabs covered in separate user stories linked to this).\nContent for all tabs except Details & Care is covered in separate user stories: \nhttps://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-102#icft=SFCC-102\n (Size & Fit), \nhttps://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-267#icft=SFCC-267\n (Shipping & Returns and Assistance), \nhttps://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-266#icft=SFCC-266\n (EU Environmental Qualities), \n[SFCC-101] PDP – Slide out - Measmerize Widget & Find My Size CTA - Jira\n (Find My Size).",
      "status": {
        "name": "Ready For Review",
        "category": "To Do",
        "color": "blue-gray"
      },
      "issue_type": {
        "name": "Story"
      },
      "labels": [
        "Custom",
        "DesignDependent",
        "PRD-008",
        "PRD-009",
        "Squad-A"
      ],
      "updated": "2026-07-31T09:29:29.628+1000"
    },
    {
      "id": "18308",
      "key": "SFCC-190",
      "summary": "PLP Inline Grid Insert – Campaign Image",
      "description": "As a\n Shopper, \nI want \nto see a large-format campaign image inserted within the product grid as I browse, \nso that \nmy browsing experience feels elevated and brand storytelling is woven into the shopping journey.\nThis story covers the PWA build of the campaign image variant of the inline grid insert component. The insert occupies a single large-format slot within the product grid on category pages, spanning 2 product rows in height, with regular product tiles filling the remaining columns alongside it. Multiple inserts on the same page alternate between left and right positioning.\nThe component can be built with mock/hardcoded content at this stage — Contentful integration is covered in SFCC-204.\nThis story is one of three covering the inline grid insert variants. The editorial image variant and featured product tile variant are covered in separate stories.\n\n\nReference Image (Figma is leading):",
      "status": {
        "name": "In Refinement",
        "category": "To Do",
        "color": "blue-gray"
      },
      "issue_type": {
        "name": "Story"
      },
      "labels": [
        "Contentful",
        "Custom",
        "DesignDependent",
        "SPR-67",
        "Squad-A"
      ],
      "updated": "2026-07-31T16:17:07.464+1000"
    },
    {
      "id": "18068",
      "key": "SFCC-82",
      "summary": "PLP – Bottom Zone: Full-Width Editorial Image Block",
      "description": "As a \nShopper, \nI want\n a full-width editorial image block to appear below the product grid on relevant category pages, \nso tha\nt I can discover curated campaign content and navigate to related collections or editorial pages.\nPicture for reference (Figma leading): \nThis story covers the PWA component shell for the full-width editorial image block. The component renders with mock/hardcoded content at this stage — Contentful integration is covered in SFCC-203. It now sits in the PLP bottom zone (but should be configurable), below the product grid and Load More button, and is only rendered when configured for a given category.",
      "status": {
        "name": "Ready For Review",
        "category": "To Do",
        "color": "blue-gray"
      },
      "issue_type": {
        "name": "Story"
      },
      "labels": [
        "DesignDependent",
        "SPR-01",
        "SPR-02",
        "SPR-05",
        "SPR-10",
        "SPR-11",
        "SPR-12",
        "SPR-13",
