===== storefront count across sources (7 vs 8) =====
.docs/architecture.md:5:Production storefront for www.zimmermann.com — multi-locale, multi-currency, eight storefronts across six regions (AU, US, UK, EU, HK, ME), with both EU and US each split into two storefronts (domestic + international).
.docs/architecture.md:251:All eight storefronts are path-prefixed on a single first-party domain and share one SFCC realm with shared customer data. The `httpOnly` SLAS refresh-token cookie set by the SSR layer is therefore presented on every storefront prefix — no cross-domain SSO bridge is needed. SLAS tokens are channel-scoped, so the SSR layer re-initialises the SLAS context per storefront; a registered shopper is silently re-recognised across a storefront switch (shared customer record), while a guest session is site-scoped and does not carry over. **The basket deliberately does not transfer across storefronts** — baskets are site-scoped and priced in the storefront's own currency/pricebook, so a shopper switching storefront starts a fresh basket. Carrying a basket across a currency boundary would produce incorrect pricing. The Global-e checkout handoff is a separate session boundary (Global-e owns its hosted checkout in full). The exact SLAS re-authorisation mechanism and the stay-signed-in UX are open items with the Salesforce integration team.
.docs/prompts/omsIntClaudeCodePrompt.md:16:Seven storefronts are in scope: AU, UK, US domestic, US international (Global-e), EU domestic,
.docs/prompts/omsIntClaudeCodePrompt.md:54:| MRT / PWA | MRT staging | 7 storefronts, Playwright matrix, Lighthouse CI |
.docs/temp/openItems.md:52:1. **`regions` content-model field.** The working assumption is that region-specific entries are filtered by a `regions` field containing the relevant SFCC site IDs. Pending content-strategy and editor-workflow sign-off — this field affects how editors author content across all eight storefronts.
.docs/integration/15-optimizely.md:60:| Storefront region | Which of the eight storefronts |
.docs/temp/tsd-architecture.md:15:- Multi-site / multi-locale routing across 8 storefronts in 6 regions
.docs/temp/tsd-architecture.md:216:All eight storefronts are path-prefixed on a single first-party domain and run on a single SFCC realm with shared customer data. This determines how a shopper's session behaves when they cross storefronts (via the country / language selector or the mismatch slide-out):
.docs/temp/tsd-architecture.md:511:E2E specs are parameterised by `SITE_ID` from day one — every journey runs across all 8 storefronts and 11 active locales, with site-specific `baseUrl`, currency, checkout owner, tax model, and consent default supplied by a fixture rather than hardcoded. (Because a test hardcoded to one region cannot be cheaply expanded later)
.docs/integration/04-omneo.md:92:- A single Omneo tenant serves all eight storefronts. Locale is passed as a query-string parameter on the iFrame URL.
.docs/integration/02-contentful.md:110:- A single Contentful Space serves all eight storefronts via Contentful's native locale model.
.docs/integration/02-contentful.md:135:1. **`regions` content-model field.** The working assumption is that region-specific entries are filtered by a `regions` field containing the relevant SFCC site IDs. Pending content-strategy and editor-workflow sign-off — this field affects how editors author content across all eight storefronts.
.docs/integration/17-measmerize.md:109:The script tag uses `id="measmerize-script"` and the `async` attribute. No server-side call or MRT proxy is needed; the script is CDN-served and the brand code is a public identifier. All eight storefronts use the widget — `data-lang-code` and `data-country-code` must be set from the storefront context on every PDP.
.docs/integration/01-sfcc.md:60:All eight storefronts are path-prefixed on a single domain and share one SFCC realm.
.docs/integration/06-booxi.md:90:- A single Booxi tenant is assumed across all eight storefronts; per-region boutique availability is configured in Booxi, not in the PWA.
.docs/integration/12-didomi.md:92:- A single Didomi Notice serves all eight storefronts; per-region purpose configuration is managed inside the Didomi Console. The Notice ID does not vary by region — Didomi auto-detects the applicable regulation from the visitor's IP.
